{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1097214-martial-arts-do-attack-successes-and-damage","id":1097214,"title":"Martial Arts/Do attack successes and damage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-26T12:22:00-07:00","id":1097214,"title":"Martial Arts/Do attack successes and damage","content":"Hello everyone. Reading both the Martial Arts and Do Abilities, I have seen that some special maneuvers add your successes in the attack roll to the damage roll. For example, the Thunder Kick damage is listed to be \u201cStrength +3 + successes\u201d (bashing damage). My question may seem obvious: do I need to add net successes (successes -1) to this formula? If my Strength was 3 and I scored 3 successes with a Thunder Kick, what would the final damage be? Nine (Str 3 +3 +3 successes)? Or eleven (Str 3 +3 +3 successes as \u201cbase damage\u201d; +2 net successes)? I find it difficult to say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2017-belgeval","name":"Belgeval","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T20:25:56-07:00","id":1097954,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say it's obvious. Thunder Kick seems to be the only Martial Arts Maneuver that specifies you add successes to damage. The rest are all listed as Strength + a flat number like 1 or 2 or whatever. They all <i>seem</i> to follow the standard rule of adding additional successes beyond the first on the attack as dice on the damage roll, with Thunder Kick seemingly the exception that doubles up on this. So either Thunder Kick gets Strength + 3 + successes + successes after the first <b>or </b>it gets Strength + 3 + successes and <i>all the other special maneuvers don't get the add successes as bonus damage dice at all.</i> It seems more likely to me that Thunder Kick was intended to double up on successes for bonus damage, but it's vague enough that your ST may rule differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T07:09:25-07:00","id":1098421,"title":"","content":"I'd say Str+3+(successes-1)+successes. So your answer is eleven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T06:35:17-07:00","id":1098745,"title":"","content":"But our attacks go to 11. Sorry couldn't resist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}